<title>BELGIUM: Dutchman appointed top EU bureaucrat.</title>
<headline>Dutchman appointed top EU bureaucrat.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission appointed Dutchman Carlo Trojan to its top administrative post on Wednesday, replacing Britain's David Williamson who is retiring as secretary general.</p>
<p>Secretary general of the Commission, the European Union's executive, is an extremely powerful position, leading the entire administration and involved in all issues.</p>
<p>Only two men have previously held the post over the 40-year history of the Commission. The first, Frenchman Emile Noel, held it from 1958 until his retirement in 1987.</p>
</text>
